# Vercel — Despliegue y configuración

## Variables de entorno

```bash
# .env.local (nunca commitear)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://[project].supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# Solo en servidor (sin NEXT_PUBLIC_)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...   # Solo admin/webhooks
```

## vercel.json

```json
{
  "framework": "nextjs",
  "buildCommand": "npm run build",
  "installCommand": "npm install",
  "regions": ["iad1"],
  "headers": [
    {
      "source": "/api/(.*)",
      "headers": [
        { "key": "X-Content-Type-Options", "value": "nosniff" },
        { "key": "X-Frame-Options", "value": "DENY" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

## next.config.ts

```typescript
import type { NextConfig } from 'next'

const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  images: {
    remotePatterns: [
      {
        protocol: 'https',
        hostname: '[project].supabase.co',
        pathname: '/storage/v1/object/public/**',
      },
    ],
  },
  experimental: {
    optimizePackageImports: ['@supabase/ssr', 'lucide-react'],
  },
}

export default nextConfig
```

## Environments

- `main` → Production → Supabase Production
- `staging` → Preview → Supabase Staging
- Feature branches → Preview → Supabase Development
- Nunca compartir `SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` entre environments

## Comandos frecuentes

```bash
supabase start
supabase db diff -f [name]
supabase db push
supabase gen types typescript --project-id [ID] > src/lib/db/types.ts

npm run dev
npm run build && npm start
npm run type-check

vercel
vercel --prod
vercel env pull .env.local
```
